---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { legal } from '../lib/data';
const updated = new Date(legal.updated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---
<Base title={`Privacy policy · ${legal.name}`} description="Privacy policy" noindex>
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This website is a simple static site. It sets no cookies, uses no analytics or
        tracking tools, shows no ads, and loads its fonts and images from its own server.
        This page explains which data is still processed when you visit it.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
      <address>
        {legal.name}<br />
        {legal.street}<br />
        {legal.city}<br />
        {legal.country}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>
      </address>

      <h2>2. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
      <p>
        This website is served by GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P.
        Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, GitHub
        processes technically necessary data, in particular your IP address, the date and
        time of the request, the requested URL, the referrer, and information about your
        browser and operating system. This data is needed to deliver the website and to
        keep the service secure. I have no access to these server logs.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is my legitimate interest in providing the website securely and
        reliably (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Data may be transferred to the USA. GitHub is
        certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, which is covered by an adequacy
        decision of the European Commission (Art. 45 GDPR). For details, see the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Theme preference stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between the light and dark theme with the moon or sun button, your
        choice is saved in your browser's local storage so that it is kept for your next
        visit. The value (<code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>) never leaves your
        device and is not sent to me or anyone else. Storing it is strictly necessary for
        this feature, which you requested (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG). You can delete it at any
        time in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        This website links to other services such as GitHub, LinkedIn, DEV and Stack
        Overflow. Simply visiting this website does not send any data to them. Their own
        privacy policies apply only once you click one of these links.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contact by email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me, I process your email address and the content of your message to
        answer your request (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, or Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your request
        relates to a contract). I delete this data once it is no longer needed for that
        purpose, unless I am legally required to keep it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
        <li>have incorrect data corrected (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
        <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
        <li>restrict processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
        <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
        <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, just send me an email. You also have the right to lodge
        a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), for
        example the <a href="https://www.baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de" rel="noopener">State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information of Baden-Württemberg</a>.
      </p>

      <p><small>Last updated: {updated}</small></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
